tt-local-generator (0.55.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * feat(create): Create now checks server readiness before launching a job.
    If the required server isn't running (or a different server is running
    on the same shared Blackhole hardware group), a confirm dialog names the
    stop/reset/start plan; only on accept does it stop the conflicting server,
    reset the boards (tt-smi -r), start the needed one, and launch the job
    once healthy. A ready server launches with no dialog, unchanged. Reuses
    `ready_to_run.plan_switch` (RN-S t1), `server_manager`,
    `pipeline_engine._tt_smi_reset`, and `ServersControl`'s log — no new
    hardware-touching code path. Confirm-before-switch is a hard safety rule
    on this hardware (a QB2 card has hard-locked the box on backend-switch
    churn before). Also fixes a latent bug in `ready_to_run.conflicting_server`:
    wrapping a real `model_status.Status` enum value in `str()` before
    lowering it returned "Status.READY" instead of "ready" (Python 3.11+
    Enum.__str__), so the live gate would never have detected a conflicting
    server — masked previously because the Task 1 tests only ever passed
    plain strings. Fixed by dropping the `str()` wrapper.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Sun, 02 Aug 2026 14:29:34 -0700

